.sp
For examples on usage of this option, please see our “using CLI with advanced JSON options” link: \fI\%https://docs.cloud.oracle.com/iaas/Content/API/SDKDocs/cliusing.htm#AdvancedJSONOptions\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-id [text]
.UNINDENT
.sp
<b>Filter</b> results by \fI\%OCID\fP <\fBhttps://docs.cloud.oracle.com/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm\fP>\&. Must be an OCID of the correct type for the resource type.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-lifecycle\-state [text]
.UNINDENT
.sp
The current state of the PipelineRun.
.sp
Accepted values are:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
ACCEPTED, CANCELED, CANCELING, DELETED, DELETING, FAILED, IN_PROGRESS, SUCCEEDED
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-limit [integer]
.UNINDENT
.sp
For list pagination. The maximum number of results per page, or items to return in a paginated “List” call. 1 is the minimum, 1000 is the maximum. See \fI\%List Pagination\fP <\fBhttps://docs.cloud.oracle.com/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/usingapi.htm#nine\fP>\&.
.sp
Example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
500
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-page [text]
.UNINDENT
.sp
For list pagination. The value of the \fIopc\-next\-page\fP response header from the previous “List” call.
.sp
See \fI\%List Pagination\fP <\fBhttps://docs.cloud.oracle.com/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/usingapi.htm#nine\fP>\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-page\-size [integer]
.UNINDENT
.sp
When fetching results, the number of results to fetch per call. Only valid when used with \fB\-\-all\fP or \fB\-\-limit\fP, and ignored otherwise.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-pipeline\-id [text]
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fI\%OCID\fP <\fBhttps://docs.cloud.oracle.com/iaas/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm\fP> of the pipeline.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by [text]
.UNINDENT
.sp
Specifies the field to sort by. Accepts only one field. By default, when you sort by \fItimeAccepted\fP, the results are shown in descending order. When you sort by \fIdisplayName\fP, the results are shown in ascending order. Sort order for the \fIdisplayName\fP field is case sensitive.
.sp
Accepted values are:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
displayName, timeAccepted
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-order [text]
.UNINDENT
.sp
Specifies sort order to use, either \fIASC\fP (ascending) or \fIDESC\fP (descending).
.sp
Accepted values are:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
ASC, DESC
.ft P
.fi
